    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "One classification drives three surfaces."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "Subsystem × severity (perception, motion planner, localization, hardware/sensor, ODD boundary × SEV1–3) powers the driver’s 1-tap tags, the hazard map, and the office incident log — no re-mapping between tools."
    },
    {
      "kind": "component",
      "name": "Dot Slider",
      "controls": {
        "dot1": "true",
        "dot2": "true",
        "dot3": "true",
        "dot4": "true",
        "dot5": "false"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "tag": "h6",
      "text": "Cross-Functional Partnership"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "Grounded every decision in how autonomy and fleet-ops teams actually work:"
    },
    {
      "kind": "list",
      "items": [
        "Safety drivers need sub-second quick-tags, not forms",
        "Ops and AV engineers need exposure and disengagement analytics after the fact",
        "Compliance needs an audit trail, not tribal knowledge"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "component",
      "name": "Dot Slider",
      "controls": {
        "dot1": "true",
        "dot2": "true",
        "dot3": "true",
        "dot4": "true",
        "dot5": "false"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "tag": "h6",
      "text": "Multi-Fidelity Prototyping"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "Proved the taxonomy before building a backend for it:"
    },
    {
      "kind": "list",
      "items": [
        "Cockpit fixture data first, labeled simulated until a real ingestion pipeline exists",
        "The office dashboard built as a second, independent consumer of the same schema",
        "Validated the taxonomy held up outside the vehicle, not just inside it"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "component",
